			},
			"date": "2025-05-28T14:44:51.968Z",
			"content": "<p>If you look at anything react-based, which is performant, like:<br>\n- stuff from poimandres<br>\n- tldraw<br>\n- motion<br>\n- tanstack<br>\n- react-three/fiber</p>\n<p>What they have in common is that they use react as keyframes, but most of the actual logic is done by ejecting from react and syncing once the actual work is done</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
